# Introduction to Johnston Engineering

Johnston Engineering (JE) is a mechanical engineering firm located in Spokane, Washington **specializing in the design, analysis, integration, ****build****, and testing of first-of-a-kind systems**. In operation since 2015, JE brings over 250 years of combined engineering experience across a team of 22, with deep expertise in system integration and advanced engineering solutions. Our work spans critical material recovery systems, industrial machinery, and biotechnology, as well as clean technology sectors including **carbon capture**, hydrogen, nuclear systems, and long-duration energy storage. 

A defining advantage of Johnston Engineering is our **Analysis-Driven Design** approach. At JE, the engineers who are designing our client’s systems are also performing physics-based simulations in thermal, structural, and fluid-flow to optimize and validate designs before we build systems. This close coupling of design and analysis ensures performance is validated before fabrication begins, preventing costly part failures and accelerating overall development timelines. We use SolidWorks to design the 3D Computer Aided Design (CAD) of our systems and ANSYS Finite Element Analysis (FEA) & Computational Fluid Dynamics (CFD) to simulate forces, pressures, torques, heat transfer and fluid interactions. We iterate through design and analysis cycles until the system has appropriate performance, modularity, reliability, serviceability and manufacturability. This helps us develop the system faster and with less risk**.** 

A second core strength is that **our ****engineers and ****designers are also ****the assemblers of ****your ****system**. The same engineers who model and analyze the system are in charge of fabrication oversight, procurement, assembly, and testing. This design and build approach is unique in the engineering world and provides our customer with two distinct advantages at the design and build phase. Our engineers and designers have developed intuitive understanding of ideal system layout, design for manufacturability & serviceability through direct hands-on experience, which provides our clients with an advantage at the design phase. At the build phase, this team continuity improves your system build because the assemblers have a deep understanding of the system layout, design intent, and system behavior. This results in faster builds and quicker issue resolution commonly occurring in first-of-a-kind systems. 

Third, we focus specifically on **first-of-a-kind (FOAK) development**. Johnston Engineering works alongside clients who are experts in their core technology but require support in transitioning systems from concept to larger implementation. Scaling a system is not a linear extension of early development as each seemingly independent decision is actually interdependent and shapes the overall system architecture. Early design choices influence cost, schedule, performance, and risk, often in compounding ways. Without informed guidance and experienced experts focused on FOAK developments, well-intentioned decisions can create downstream challenges that are expensive and time-consuming to correct.

Our niche is system scale-up and we do it every day.  This focus on FOAK systems has resulted in a team with an intuitive understanding of the implications of component and system architecture decisions that affect the cost, complexity, and schedule of projects.  We support technologies across TRL 3 to 9 and regularly help clients move from promising concepts to integrated subsystems, to pilot-scale systems, and finally field-deployable hardware.

These three strengths of Analysis Driven design, hands on experience, and focus on FOAK systems make up Johnston Engineering’s design-analysis-build-test approach.

JE President, Andy Johnston, P.E., leads the team at JE and provides subject-matter expertise in structural, thermal, and fluid flow analysis, with over 20 years of experience in advanced thermal-management systems, energy technologies, aerospace and defense. Before founding Johnston Engineering, Andy spent 11 years at Parker Aerospace Thermal Management Systems designing liquid heating, cooling, and environmental control systems for military and aerospace platforms. 

To date, JE has completed more than 190 FOAK engineering projects including 25 projects for the U.S. Department of Energy, and balance in private industry.** JE has ****successfully ****completed 1****4**** ****Carbon Capture Utilization and Storage (CCUS) ****projects,**** and our design-analysis-build-test approach makes us an ideal partner to develop Nitto’s Mobile Demonstration Unit**

The following sections of the proposal will first provide examples of Johnston Engineering’s previous work then provide information specific to Nitto’s Mobile Demonstration Unit including Scope, Deliverables, pricing and timing.  

