## Project Timeline

The complete project duration is 173 labor days. Assuming 1 staff per labor category and standard lead times, if the project kicks off at the beginning of January 2026, **the project ****can be completed by ****end of Q2**** ****or early Q3 ****2026.**** ****  **

Johnston Engineering has the capacity to increase staffing if an accelerated schedule is desired. While adding personnel can shorten the overall timeline, increasing team size means more engineers must review and digest the same information, attend meetings, etc. resulting in natural duplication of some effort. For this reason, an expedited timeline may increase labor costs by approximately 5%-10% for approximately a 25% increase in delivery speed. 

## Pricing and Billing Process

This proposal is based on a time and material (T&M) hourly rate of $205 for time and a 25% markup for materials. 

Johnston Engineering works from a retainer payment agreement. All services are pre-paid in monthly reserved hours. Unused hours do not expire and will roll over to the following month. At every invoice cycle, Johnston Engineering provides the Client with its current positive or negative balance and makes recommendations for future hourly purchases. All invoices are due on receipt. Upon project completion, any remaining hours can be used for future projects or refunded at the sole discretion of the client.

Our billing process is broken down into detailed categories allowing Nitto to see exactly how much time was spent on each task. For each labor charge, invoices will detail the date, labor category, description of work performed, and hours used. For materials charges, invoices will detail the date, description of the hardware, and cost.

